  "about": "The dock as one surface (docs/adr/0034-the-dock.mdx, 5 November 2026), dark, on the ThinkPad's display (1600×1000 at 1.25) with the session's shell, beside Bloom's SettingsLayout in a window (sample/WindowProbe.tsx): flush with the display's sides and bottom with no outline, its top corners round while no window is zoomed (the wallpaper above each curve, its anti-aliased pixels between the wallpaper and the shelf, the shelf's own colour (#1d1f24) to the level just inside it, along its top and down to its bottom row and sides), square while the window is zoomed to the work area by its green bubble (the shelf's colour in its very corner pixels, the window's last row right above it, no desktop between them), and round again restored; its radii going from 28 to 0 as it zooms and back as it restores monotonically over the frames between (the zoom's spring, the shell's report of its commits). Dropsea's and Atlas's icons are their own pictures to their tiles' edges. With the corners square throughout (the note of 3 November), round beside the zoomed window, changed at once, a border on the shelf (a rounded bordered background kept 0.8 px inside every edge, as Android's: the wallpaper down its sides and along its bottom), or the icons on white circles with a ring, it fails.",
